Let's take the `PUT_AddContract` method as an example. It's assumed that x is being added to the ArrayList and its Count is increased accordingly. Here's how you could generate the corresponding assert:

```cs
[PexMethod]
public void PUT_AddContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int Old_x = x;
    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    int New_Ret = arrList.Add(x);

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1); // Asserts that Count property increased by 1
    Assert.IsTrue(New_Ret == Old_arrListCount); // Asserts that Add method returns the index of the new item
    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListIndexOfX == Old_arrListIndexOfX); // Asserts that IndexOf returns the same index before and after add operation
    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListLastIndexOfX == Old_arrListLastIndexOfX); // Asserts that LastIndexOf returns the same index before and after add operation
    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListContainsX == true); // Asserts that Contains returns true

    // You can continue for other conditions...
}
```

This is just a simple example and actual assert statements may vary depending on what specific conditions you are testing. Please provide more specific details if you need more detailed help!
